    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Dewey Prairie Baptist Church began in 1886, and a post office named Donie opened in 1898 after a misreading.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/donie-tx",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1907 the Trinity and Brazos Valley Railway built a line east of town, prompting residents to relocate.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/donie-tx",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "By 1969 Donie had 230 residents, seven businesses, three churches, a school, and the Donie Chair Company, famed for colonial‑style chairs shipped across the Southwest.",
